<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Jai Singh I</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1611">1611</a>–<a href="/years/1667">1667</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a> · Also known as Mirza Raja Jai Singh</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Jai Singh I, known as Mirza Raja, was the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kachhwaha">Kachwaha</a> ruler of Amber in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rajasthan">Rajasthan</a> from 1621 and one of the leading generals of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mughal-empire">Mughal Empire</a>. Serving <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shah-jahan">Shah Jahan</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aurangzeb">Aurangzeb</a>, he forced the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maratha-empire">Maratha</a> leader <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shivaji">Shivaji</a> to accept the Treaty of Purandar in 1665 and then led an unsuccessful campaign against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/adil-shahi-dynasty">Bijapur Sultanate</a> in 1665–1666. He died at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/burhanpur">Burhanpur</a> in 1667.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/jai-singh-i.jpg" alt="Jai Singh I" width="320" height="580" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Jai_Singh_I.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
